                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7e9ea064-2e33-4542-8305-54c2c5043b52",
                        "source_entry_id": "ce7705fc-af80-3008-81e6-b1de87314c9c",
                        "source_sense_id": "b6fed9f6-552a-3383-83e4-38e342b9fd7e",
                        "source_sense_description": "verklebter Reis",
                        "target_lang_word": "sticky rice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sticky rice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2a03902a-4864-3796-b562-6afa4ba34309",
                                        "entry_id": "12d254f8-5664-3f13-88a2-6324642a4c0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A variety of short-grain rice popular in South and East Asia, known for its stickiness when cooked."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "aa717a8d-0a7a-333a-9c1d-5802bb0ecafb",
                                        "entry_id": "12d254f8-5664-3f13-88a2-6324642a4c0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An (East) Asian man who is mostly attracted to other Asian men."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "885d2868-750b-458d-b87e-1b0d1fed7885",
                                                "sense_id": "aa717a8d-0a7a-333a-9c1d-5802bb0ecafb",
                                                "text": "I think they are changing now, too, though, because you see groups and groups of them in bars, all Asian, together. It’s amazing. So my market is much more expanded. I’m “sticky rice” [Asians who like Asians]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a476903-03fb-43df-873f-651fa6a654ec",
                                                "sense_id": "aa717a8d-0a7a-333a-9c1d-5802bb0ecafb",
                                                "text": "During my \"sticky rice\" phase, I explored what it meant to be queer and Asian in contemporary America. We had terms for everyone: if you were rice (gay and Asian) and you liked white men, then you were a snow queen or a potato queen. White men who liked you were called rice queens. Every ethnicity had a term, usually related to food."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3eb21449-7de1-4da9-82dd-cd97a472abf3",
                                                "sense_id": "aa717a8d-0a7a-333a-9c1d-5802bb0ecafb",
                                                "text": "For instance, a rice queen is a white man who likes Asians. Asian men hooking up with Asian men are described as rice that sticks to other rice. Depending on the context, sticky rice can easily be resignified from a term of empowerment into a term of insult."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2b377ba0-7fa4-439b-9cb0-9f8352f84e96",
                        "source_entry_id": "ce7705fc-af80-3008-81e6-b1de87314c9c",
                        "source_sense_id": "b6fed9f6-552a-3383-83e4-38e342b9fd7e",
                        "source_sense_description": "verklebter Reis",
                        "target_lang_word": "riz gluant",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "riz gluant",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4cb30cc3-a75f-34ff-8966-11a5f1396d4c",
                                        "entry_id": "a3dbd292-7140-329b-9924-fd58a7331e35",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nom vulgaire de Oryza sativa var. glutinosa, et de ses graines de couleur noire ou rouge, variété de riz caractérisé par un faible taux d’amylose et par sa teneur élevée en amylopectine qui le rend gluant, collant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6127adc0-0f59-43ae-8826-8eac5f1557ec",
                                                "sense_id": "4cb30cc3-a75f-34ff-8966-11a5f1396d4c",
                                                "text": "De même, savourer le dessert traditionnel « niangao », composé de riz gluant et d’haricots rouges, est un gage de bonne croissance pour les enfants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3226fa4c-14f4-4284-af9a-8d3c145946b5",
                                                "sense_id": "4cb30cc3-a75f-34ff-8966-11a5f1396d4c",
                                                "text": "Derrière l’euphorie du moment, les achats d’arbres fruitiers pour décorer les maisons ainsi que la confection des traditionnels banh chung (ces gâteaux de riz gluant fourrés au germe de soya et au porc), le scénario est ici difficile à esquiver."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bb11be9-0092-4566-b56c-216a09465b54",
                                                "sense_id": "4cb30cc3-a75f-34ff-8966-11a5f1396d4c",
                                                "text": "Le riz gluant représente 85 % de la production de riz au Laos. Alors que dans beaucoup de pays asiatiques le riz gluant est utilisé pour la confection d’alcool et de gâteaux, sa consommation quotidienne comme aliment de base est spécifique du Laos et du nord-est de la Thaïlande, d’une partie des États shan de Birmanie et certaines populations du nord-ouest du Vietnam et du sud de la Chine (Yunnan méridional et Guangxi occidental)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
